.TH OSHOT 1 "2026-10-14" "oshot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oshot \- screenshot overlay that extracts text and scans QR codes and barcodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oshot
.RI [ OPTIONS ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oshot
captures the screen and opens an overlay to select a region of it.
The selection can be read with Tesseract OCR, scanned for QR codes and
barcodes with ZBar, annotated, and copied to the clipboard or saved.
.PP
Without options, oshot captures the screen, opens the overlay and then
stays in the system tray.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and other information about the build.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-source " \fIPATH\fR"
Use the image at \fIPATH\fR instead of capturing the screen.
Use \fB\-\fR to read the image from standard input.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Use the config file at \fIPATH\fR
(default: \fI~/.config/oshot/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-override " \fIOPTION\fR"
Override a config option, for example
\fB"delay=200"\fR or \fB"default.ocr-model='jpn'"\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delay " \fIMILLIS\fR"
Wait \fIMILLIS\fR milliseconds before capturing the screen.
Has no effect with \fB\-f\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-instant\-copy ", " \-\-instant\-save [=\fIDIR\fR]
Copy or save the selection as soon as it is made. With \fIDIR\fR, save it
there without asking, named after the \fBimage-out-fmt\fR option; \fIDIR\fR is
created if it doesn't exist.
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-text
Print the text of the screenshot, or of the \fB\-f\fR image, recognized with OCR,
without opening the overlay. With \fB\-\-instant\-copy\fR, copy it to the
clipboard instead. Exits with status 1 if no text is found.
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-barcode
Like \fB\-\-extract\-text\fR, for QR codes and barcodes: prints the content of
each one found, one per line.
.TP
.BR \-\-selection " \fIREGION\fR"
Use only \fIREGION\fR of the screenshot or image, in its pixels, given as
\fIW\fRx\fIH\fR+\fIX\fR+\fIY\fR (as printed by
.BR slop (1))
or "\fIX\fR,\fIY\fR \fIW\fRx\fIH\fR" (as printed by
.BR slurp (1)).
Needs \fB\-\-extract\-text\fR, \fB\-\-extract\-barcode\fR, \fB\-\-instant\-copy\fR
or \fB\-\-instant\-save\fR, and skips the overlay. \fB\-\-instant\-save\fR then
saves without asking, to \fIDIR\fR or else the folder an image was last saved
to (by default the Pictures folder), and prints the file's path.
.PP
These options are meant for scripts: they never open a window, dialog or
notification, print errors on stderr, and exit with status 1 on failure.
.TP
.BR \-\-gen\-config " [\fIPATH\fR]"
Generate the default config file at \fIPATH\fR, or at the default location
if omitted. Asks before overwriting.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gui
Only capture and open the overlay, without the system tray.
Bind this to a key in the desktop or window manager settings to get a
capture shortcut.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tray
Only start in the system tray, without capturing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TESSDATA_PREFIX
Directory with the Tesseract \fI.traineddata\fR models.
Takes precedence over the \fBocr\-path\fR config option, unless
\fBconfig\-over\-env\fR is enabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oshot/config.toml
The config file. \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is used instead of \fI~/.config\fR
when set.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oshot/theme.toml
The theme file.
.SH NOTES
On Wayland the screen is captured through the desktop's screenshot portal,
Spectacle on KDE, or
.BR grim (1)
where no portal is available. Copying to the clipboard needs
.BR wl\-copy (1)
on Wayland and
.BR xclip (1)
on X11.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR zbarimg (1)
.PP
https://github.com/Toni500github/oshot
